    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The Aga Khan University (AKU) today inaugurated the first academic facilities and student residences of its new 60-acre campus in Kampala, Uganda. The ceremony, which also marked the start of construction of the Aga Khan University Hospital, Kampala was presided over by its Chancellor, His Highness the Aga Khan, and President of Uganda Yoweri Kaguta Museveni. The project is among the largest investments AKU has made in East Africa to date.",
